        "comments": "The assembly cbBryMarr1.1 is based on 92x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. A large number of repeats is in the unlocalised sequences. Hi-C contact map indicates a diploid-like pattern with homologous signal between pairs of chromosomes, suggesting the genome is a degenerated allo-diploid.",
